 Deployment helpers for the internal services.
 
-`bin/notify-deploy.sh SERVICE VERSION` restarts the service on the deploy host and posts a
-message to the release channel. The webhook URL comes from `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` in the
-environment; per-service settings live in `etc/services.conf`.
+`bin/notify-deploy.sh [--dry-run] SERVICE VERSION [NOTE]` restarts the service on the deploy
+host and posts a message to the release channel. The webhook URL comes from `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL`
+in the environment; per-service settings live in `etc/services.conf`.
+
+- `SERVICE` must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}$` and `VERSION` must match
+  `^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._+-]{0,63}$`; anything else is rejected (exit 65).
+- `NOTE` (optional) is a short release note, at most 500 characters with no control characters.
+  It is appended to the Slack message: `Deployed web 1.4.2 by alice: fixes login timeout`.
+  Quote it so the shell passes it as one argument.
+- `--dry-run` prints what the script would do (the remote command and the Slack message) and
+  exits without restarting the service or posting. It does not need `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL`, and the
+  flag may appear anywhere in the argument list.
+
+```sh
+bin/notify-deploy.sh --dry-run web 1.4.2 "fixes login timeout"
+bin/notify-deploy.sh web 1.4.2 "fixes login timeout"
+```
